@scene chapter_2_trial_of_choice

background: valley_vista.jpg
music: mystery_forest.mp3

dialogue:
"You step through the doorway."
"Behind you, the endless hall folds shut like a closing book."
"The last of the Sage's floating chests wink out, one by one."
"Warm air fills your lungs — real air, with weather in it."
"And a whole world opens up beneath you."
"Green valleys. A river threading between farmland. Mountains standing in the far haze."
"After an eternity of shelves and lamplight, the sky feels impossibly wide."

npc You:
"So this is what was on the other side of the door."

background: green_valley.jpg

dialogue:
"You follow the path down into the valley."
"Long grass brushes your knees. Wildflowers lean out of the verge."
"For a while there is nothing to do but walk, and it is the first easy thing that has happened to you."
"Far ahead, a dark treeline waits at the valley's edge."

npc You:
"The Sage said someone was waiting."

background: deep_forest.jpg

dialogue:
"The trees close over you, and the light goes green and dim."
"Twisted branches lock overhead, casting long shadows across the forest floor."
"A narrow path reveals itself between the trunks."
"You take a cautious step forward."
"Then another."
"The silence is unsettling."
"Not a bird sings."
"Not a leaf rustles."
"Only the sound of your own footsteps echoes through the woods."
"..."
"Suddenly—"

npc Unknown:
"AAAGH!"

dialogue:
"A cry of pain pierces the silence."
"Without thinking, you sprint toward the voice."
"Branches whip past your face as you race deeper into the forest."
"The trees suddenly part..."

background: forest_gate.png

dialogue:
"Before you stands an enormous stone gate, carved into the side of an ancient mountain."
"The gate is covered in glowing runes that pulse with mysterious energy."
"At its base lies an elderly man wrapped in a worn, tattered cloak."

background: elder_mage.png

dialogue:
"He appears to be in his eighties."
"His breathing is heavy."
"He struggles to remain conscious."
"You kneel beside him."

npc You:
"Sir! Are you alright?"

dialogue:
"The old man slowly opens his eyes."
"A faint smile appears on his face."

npc Old Man:
"Traveller..."

dialogue:
"He coughs before continuing."

npc Old Man:
"Please... help me."
"I have spent decades trying to open it..."
"...but age has finally caught up with me."
"If you help me unlock this gate..."
"...I shall repay you with something far more valuable than treasure."

dialogue:
"He looks directly into your eyes."

npc Old Man:
"Knowledge."

background: forest_gate.png

dialogue:
"The glowing runes across the gate suddenly begin to shine."
"The ground trembles."
"Ancient symbols appear before you."

system notification:
"NEW QUEST"
"TRIAL OF CHOICE"
"Teach the gate how to decide."

dialogue:
"The old man slowly rises to his feet, leaning on his wooden staff."
"He places his hand upon the gate."
"Three ancient symbols ignite."
"🔥 Fire"
"🌊 Water"
"🌿 Nature"
"The symbols float in the air, waiting."
"The old man begins to explain."

npc Old Man:
"This is the Gate of Choices."
"Unlike the trials before, strength alone cannot open it."
"This gate obeys only one law..."
"...the law of decisions."

dialogue:
"He traces three glowing lines in the air."
"Each line connects to one of the symbols."

npc Old Man:
"You already carry the spells you need, {{player_name}}."
"input() — to ask the traveller for a number."
"print() — to declare which path opens."
"What you lack is the power to CHOOSE between them."

dialogue:
"He taps the gate twice with his staff."

npc Old Man:
"The gate will present a number."
"If the number is 1, the path of Fire must open."
"If the number is 2, the path of Water must open."
"If the number is 3, the path of Nature must open."

dialogue:
"He pauses."
"The symbols suddenly dim."

npc Old Man:
"But beware..."
"If the traveler enters any other number..."
"...the gate must reject the choice."

dialogue:
"The ancient runes rearrange themselves into a glowing command."
"[Enter a number between 1, 2 and 3.]"
"The old man turns toward you."

npc Old Man:
"The gate cannot think for itself."
"It follows only the instructions it is given."
"You must teach it how to choose."

dialogue:
"The runes begin assembling into lines of unfinished code."

system system:
"MISSION"
"Write an if / elif / else statement."
"1 → Fire · 2 → Water · 3 → Nature"
"Anything else → 'Enter number between 1, 2 and 3.'"

dialogue:
"The old man steps back."
"The gate waits in silence."
"Only your code can decide which path will open."

mission: trial_of_choice
